      "explanation": "‘I doubt whether that was true of Charlotte Brontë’ was rendered as its opposite; corrected."
    },
    {
      "segment": "woolf-a-room-of-one-s-own:6.22",
      "category": "semantic_fidelity",
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "explanation": "‘a whole nine years ago’ lost its irony (‘mới đây đúng chín năm’); now ‘đã trọn chín năm rồi’."
    },
    {
      "segment": "woolf-a-room-of-one-s-own:6.5",
      "category": "semantic_fidelity",
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "resolved",
      "explanation": "The English capital letter ‘I’, Woolf’s emblem of male egotism, was left unexplained; a short gloss was added."
    },
