  "summary": "Full assessment of all 155 English/Vietnamese passages: chapter headings ONE–SIX and every paragraph, from the Oxbridge lawn and the luncheon to Shakespeare’s sister, Mary Carmichael and the closing appeal. The first reviews scored 8.725 and 8.125 and found a major each in a later round (four majors in all, three inverted or flattened statements and one unglossed English-only image), each fixed and re-checked; the last fresh reviews scored 8.65 (units 1–69) and 8.625 (units 70–155) with no major or critical finding. On the half-point scale the final score is 8.625, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
